\section{Asymmetric Axis: Signed y-Tilt Sweep}

\Cref{fig:y-tilt-asym} shows the asymmetry ratio
$|F_z(+2.5^{\circ}_y)| / |F_z(-2.5^{\circ}_y)|$ as a function of depth,
on a logarithmic axis.

\begin{figure}[h]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.85\linewidth]{finray_26_y_tilt_asymmetry.png}
\caption[Asymmetry vs depth]{Asymmetry ratio between $+2.5^{\circ}$ and
$-2.5^{\circ}$ y-tilts as a function of press depth for
\texttt{finray\_26}. The finray exhibits strong directional ``handedness''
at boundary depths but loses it in the soft plateau.}
\label{fig:y-tilt-asym}
\end{figure}

At $-1.0$\,mm, the ratio is $2.36\times$---force at $+2.5^{\circ}$
($-8.00$\,N) is more than double the force at $-2.5^{\circ}$ ($-3.39$\,N).
At $-0.5$\,mm, the ratio is $1.38\times$. At $+10$\,mm, the ratio is
$1.009\times$, statistically indistinguishable from $1$.

\Cref{tab:y-tilt-asym} reports the absolute values along with $0^{\circ}$
baselines where available.

